 "notes": "Headline limit: 2-sigma (Delta chi^2=4) exclusion from the double-narrow-line (two-peak) analysis of 284.7 ks XRISM/Resolve data on the Centaurus cluster (A3526), Fig. 3 left recast to the ALP-photon coupling in Fig. 4 left (figALP.pdf). Curve extracted from the vector PDF: ~16k plotted dots trace a rapidly oscillating limit; reported points are the lower envelope (5th percentile per 0.125 keV bin, 100 bins over 3.6-16.1 keV), i.e. the visible lower edge of the plotted exclusion region; the local curve fluctuates up to ~2-3x above this envelope. Conversion in paper: Gamma^-1 = 4.2e24 yr (1e-18 GeV^-1/g)^2 (keV/m)^3 with q=2, matching L=-(g/4)aFF~, so g is directly g_agamma. Astrophysical decay limit (NFW profiles: cluster rho_s=0.025 GeV/cm^3, MW rho_s=0.46 GeV/cm^3); no local-DM-density rescaling applied. XMM-Newton blank-sky curve in the same figure is a comparison from another paper, not included.",
